  "_comment": "Normalised SHA-256 pins for PE images whose bytes legitimately move. Produced by tools/gate/pin_pe_normalised.py; see that file for which fields are masked and why, and for the measurement showing a plain hash cannot work here. Keyed by repo-relative PATH, not filename: the same library ships at several paths with different content. Valid for repeated builds of the same tree with the same toolchain -- NOT across machines, because __FILE__ embeds the absolute source path.",
  "_pdfe_exe_deliberately_absent": "pdfe.exe is NOT pinned here, on purpose. Its normalised hash changes on every legitimate change to linked code, i.e. most commits, so a committed snapshot of it would go red for ordinary work with no way to tell that apart from a nondeterministic build -- the noisy_guard_masks_everything shape, and a guard that reds routinely gets silenced. The karen gate failed phase-11 of pipeline p96-open-issues for exactly that. GitHub #298's reproducibility property is instead asserted by building TWICE and comparing the two outputs to each other, in tests/test_pe_rebuild_determinism.py -- no snapshot, so nothing to go stale. The entries that remain are vcpkg-cache-sourced DLLs, whose bytes are stable until a cache entry changes.",
